module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierAffineLocal.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierAffineLocalConverse.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalCone.ConormalSymmetricChart
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalCone.EffectiveCartierConormalSheaf

/-!
# The canonical map out of the symmetric algebra is an isomorphism for an effective Cartier divisor

[Stacks, Tag 0632] gives the canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` of graded algebras and says
it is surjective, and an isomorphism in degrees zero and one. This file proves that it is an
isomorphism in **every** degree when the ideal of the immersion is locally generated by a
nonzerodivisor — the local shape of an effective Cartier divisor, [Stacks, Tag 01WS] — and
deduces it for an effective Cartier divisor.

Only injectivity is at issue, surjectivity being `Stacks.Conormal.epi_conormalSymmetricHom_app`.
The argument is local and has two halves, both already proved:

* over a chart on which `ℐ(U) = (f)` with `f` a nonzerodivisor, `ℐⁿ/ℐⁿ⁺¹` is free of rank one on
  the class of `fⁿ` (`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalCone.ConormalPowerChart`);
* over the same chart every section of the *sectionwise* degree-`n` symmetric power is a multiple
  of the `n`-fold product of the degree-one class of `f`, and the canonical map carries that
  product to the class of `fⁿ`
  (`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.NormalCone.ConormalSymmetricChart`).

A section of `Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` comes from the sectionwise symmetric power only locally, so the two
halves are joined by two applications of separatedness: one to descend to the opens where a
section lifts along the sheafification unit, and one to descend from those to the charts.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Conormal.HasPrincipalChartBasis`: the charts with a principal nonzerodivisor ideal form
  a basis of opens of the source.
* `Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis`: **the canonical
  map is injective on the sections over every open**, in every degree, under that hypothesis.
* `Stacks.Conormal.isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis`: **the canonical map
  is an isomorphism in every degree**, under that hypothesis.
* `Stacks.Conormal.hasPrincipalChartBasis_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`: **an effective Cartier
  divisor has a principal nonzerodivisor chart basis.**
* `Stacks.Conormal.isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`: **for an
  effective Cartier divisor the canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{D/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{D/X,*}` is an isomorphism in
  every degree.**

## Implementation notes

### Two spellings of the functions on a chart

The sections of a sectionwise symmetric power are a module over
`(Z.sheaf.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op V)`, and the sections of a homogeneous piece
of the conormal algebra are a module over `Z.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op V)`. The two rings are
definitionally equal and neither instance is found for the other spelling, so no statement below
mentions a scalar acting on both; the identity that crosses the seam is proved as a term, which is
the same device as in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SymmetricSituation.DegreeOneGeneration`.

### No `@[stacks 0637]`

Tag 0637 asserts of the morphism `C_ZX ⟶ N_ZX` that it exists, that it is a closed immersion and
that it is a morphism of cones; this file bears on none of those three clauses directly. What it
supplies is the input that the morphism is an *isomorphism* for an effective Cartier divisor,
which is the hypothesis the zero section of the normal line cone of [Stacks, Tag 0FEB] needs and
which Tag 0637 does not state.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0632](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0632)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Conormal

variable {Z X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Local injectivity over a principal chart -/

/-- **Over a principal chart with a nonzerodivisor generator the canonical map is injective on
the sections coming from the sectionwise symmetric power.** Both sections are multiples of the
`n`-fold product of the degree-one class of `f`, the canonical map carries such a multiple to the
same multiple of the class of `fⁿ`, and that class is annihilated by no nonzero function.

The two `letI`s give the functions on the chart, in the spelling the sectionwise symmetric powers
are modules over, their action on the two sheaves the canonical map relates; they are the
instances already present for the other spelling of the same ring, and they are what lets one
`map_smul` serve on both sides of the canonical map. -/
private theorem eq_of_app_sheafifyUnit_eq {i : Z ⟶ X} [IsImmersion i] (U : X.affineOpens)
    (hU : IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl)) {f : Γ(X, U.1)}
    (hf : chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span {f}) (hfreg : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U.1)) (n : ℕ)
    (a b : (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ)
      (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
    (h : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
        (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
          (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
            (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) a) =
      PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
        (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
          (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
            (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) b)) :
    a = b := by
  let : Module ((Z.sheaf.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      (((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Module (Z.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      (((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))))
  let : Module ((Z.sheaf.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafifyRestrict (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ)
          (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val)).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Module (Z.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafifyRestrict (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ)
          (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val)).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))))
  let : Module ((Z.sheaf.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      (((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) :=
    inferInstanceAs (Module (Z.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)))
      (((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))))
  have e : ∀ c : (Z.sheaf.obj ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)),
      PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
          (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
            (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
              (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
            (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) (c • chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n)) =
        c • (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU n (chartIdealPowGen i U hf n) := by
    intro c
    have hA : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
          (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
            (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) (c • chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n) =
        c • PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
          (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
            (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) (chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n) := by
      rw [map_smul]
    have hB : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
          (c • PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
            (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
              (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
            (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) (chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n)) =
        c • PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
          (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
          (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
            (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
              (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
            (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) (chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n)) :=
      map_smul _ c _
    exact (congrArg (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val
        (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) hA).trans (hB.trans (congrArg (fun y => c • y)
      (conormalSymmetricHom_app_sheafifyUnit_prod i U hU hf n)))
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := exists_smul_chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n a
  obtain ⟨r', hr'⟩ := exists_smul_chartSymmetricProd i U hU hf n b
  have key : r • (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU n (chartIdealPowGen i U hf n) =
      r' • (conormalAlgebra i).localMap U hU n (chartIdealPowGen i U hf n) := by
    rw [← e r, ← e r', hr, hr', h]
  rw [← hr, ← hr', ((conormalAlgebra i).bijective_smul_localMap_pow U hU hf hfreg n).1 key]

/-! ### The principal chart basis -/

/-- **The charts with a principal nonzerodivisor ideal form a basis of opens of the source.**
Every point of every open of `Z` lies in the preimage of an affine open `U` of `X` inside that
open, on which `i` restricts to a closed immersion and on which the chart ideal is generated by a
single nonzerodivisor. This is the local shape of an effective Cartier divisor,
[Stacks, Tag 01WS]. -/
def HasPrincipalChartBasis (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i] : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : Z.Opens) (x : Z), x ∈ V →
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, IsClosedImmersion (i.resLE U.1 (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) le_rfl) ∧
      ∃ f : Γ(X, U.1), x ∈ i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ∧ i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ V ∧
        chartIdeal i U = Ideal.span {f} ∧ f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U.1)

/-! ### Injectivity, and the isomorphism -/

/-- **The canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` is injective on the sections over every
open**, in every nonnegative degree, when the principal nonzerodivisor charts form a basis.

Two sections with the same image agree after restriction to any open on which both lift along the
sheafification unit, because there they agree on every principal chart by
`Stacks.Conormal.eq_of_app_sheafifyUnit_eq`; the opens where both lift cover, so separatedness of
`Symⁿ(𝒞_{Z/X})` finishes. -/
theorem injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hb : HasPrincipalChartBasis i) (n : ℕ) (V : Z.Opens) :
    Function.Injective (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op V)) := by
  intro u v h
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext
    ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).isSheaf (U := op V) ?_
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨W₁, g₁, hg₁, hxW₁⟩ := Stacks.liftSieve_mem (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
    (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) u x hx
  obtain ⟨W₂, g₂, hg₂, hxW₂⟩ := Stacks.liftSieve_mem (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
    (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) v x hx
  obtain ⟨U, hU, f, hxU, hUW, hgen, hfreg⟩ := hb (W₁ ⊓ W₂) x ⟨hxW₁, hxW₂⟩
  have hW1 : i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ W₁ := hUW.trans inf_le_left
  have hW2 : i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ W₂ := hUW.trans inf_le_right
  have hWV : i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ V := hW1.trans g₁.le
  have hS : ∀ (s) {W : Z.Opens} (g : W ⟶ V), Stacks.liftSieve (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
      (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) s g →
      i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ W → Stacks.liftSieve (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) s
        (homOfLE hWV) := by
    intro s W g hg hle
    have h0 := (Stacks.liftSieve (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
      (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) s).downward_closed
        hg (homOfLE hle)
    rwa [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE hle ≫ g) (homOfLE hWV)] at h0
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Stacks.exists_lift_of_liftSieve (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
    (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) u
    (homOfLE hWV) (hS u g₁ hg₁ hW1)
  obtain ⟨b, hbl⟩ := Stacks.exists_lift_of_liftSieve (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
    (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val) v
    (homOfLE hWV) (hS v g₂ hg₂ hW2)
  have hu : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
      (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) a =
    ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hWV).op u := ha
  have hv : PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
      (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) b =
    ((conormalSymmetricAlgebra i).piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hWV).op v := hbl
  refine ⟨i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1, hWV, hxU, ?_⟩
  refine Eq.trans hu.symm (Eq.trans (congrArg (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
      (PresheafOfModules.sheafifyUnit (𝟙 Z.ringCatSheaf.obj)
        (PresheafOfModules.symPowInt (n : ℤ) (conormalSheafDegreeOne i).val))
      (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) (eq_of_app_sheafifyUnit_eq U hU hgen hfreg n a b ?_)) hv)
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
    ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) hu) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (homOfLE hWV).op u) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun y =>
    ((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece (n : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hWV).op y) h) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (homOfLE hWV).op v).symm ?_
  exact congrArg (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
    ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (n : ℤ)).val (op (i ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) hv.symm

/-- **The canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{Z/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X,*}` is an isomorphism in every degree** when the
principal nonzerodivisor charts form a basis of opens of the source: it is a monomorphism by
`Stacks.Conormal.injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis` and an epimorphism
by `Stacks.Conormal.epi_conormalSymmetricHom_app`. In a negative degree both sides vanish. -/
theorem isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis (i : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion i]
    (hb : HasPrincipalChartBasis i) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app n) := by
  rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with hn | hn
  · refine ⟨0, ?_, ?_⟩
    · exact (Scheme.Modules.isZero_symmetricAlgebra_piece Z
        ((conormalAlgebra i).algebra.piece 1) n hn).eq_of_src _ _
    · exact ((conormalAlgebra i).negative_isZero n hn).eq_of_src _ _
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le hn
  have : Mono ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (m : ℤ)) :=
    (SheafOfModules.forget Z.ringCatSheaf).mono_of_mono_map
      (PresheafOfModules.mono_of_injective (f := ((conormalSymmetricHom i).app (m : ℤ)).val)
        fun W => injective_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis i hb m W.unop)
  have := epi_conormalSymmetricHom_app i (m : ℤ)
  exact isIso_of_mono_of_epi _

/-! ### The case of an effective Cartier divisor -/

/-- **An effective Cartier divisor has a principal nonzerodivisor chart basis.** Around the image
of a point of `D` there is an affine open on which the ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor
(`Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor`); shrinking it inside a given open
keeps both properties, by `Stacks.Divisors.ker_app_eq_span_res` and
`Stacks.CartierAffineLocalConverse.nonZeroDivisor_res`. -/
theorem hasPrincipalChartBasis_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D) :
    HasPrincipalChartBasis D.subschemeι := by
  intro V x hx
  obtain ⟨U₀, hxU₀, hU₀V, hU₀cob⟩ := exists_affineChart_mem D.subschemeι V x hx
  obtain ⟨U₁, hxU₁, f₁, hf₁, hgen₁⟩ :=
    Stacks.CartierAffineLocal.exists_affineOpen_nonZeroDivisor D hD (D.subschemeι x)
  obtain ⟨-, ⟨U, hUaff, rfl⟩, hxU, hUle⟩ :=
    X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (show D.subschemeι x ∈ (U₀.1 : Set X) ∩ (U₁.1 : Set X) from ⟨hxU₀, hxU₁⟩)
      (U₀.1.2.inter U₁.1.2)
  have hUU₀ : (⟨U, hUaff⟩ : X.affineOpens).1 ≤ U₀.1 := fun y hy => (hUle hy).1
  have hUU₁ : (⟨U, hUaff⟩ : X.affineOpens).1 ≤ U₁.1 := fun y hy => (hUle hy).2
  refine ⟨⟨U, hUaff⟩,
    isClosedImmersion_resLE_of_le_coborderRange D.subschemeι U (hUU₀.trans hU₀cob),
    (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUU₁).op).hom f₁, hxU, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact fun y hy => hU₀V (hUU₀ hy)
  · exact Stacks.Divisors.ker_app_eq_span_res D U₁.2
      (isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors.2 hf₁) hgen₁ U hUU₁
  · exact Stacks.CartierAffineLocalConverse.nonZeroDivisor_res (V := U₁) (f := f₁)
      (hf := hf₁) (i := homOfLE hUU₁)

/-- **For an effective Cartier divisor the canonical map `Sym*(𝒞_{D/X}) ⟶ 𝒞_{D/X,*}` of
[Stacks, Tag 0632] is an isomorphism in every degree.** This is the input which, together with
invertibility of `𝒞_{D/X,1}`, says that the normal cone of an effective Cartier divisor is the
line bundle of its conormal sheaf. -/
theorem isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    [hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D] (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((conormalSymmetricHom D.subschemeι).app n) :=
  isIso_conormalSymmetricHom_app_of_hasPrincipalChartBasis D.subschemeι
    (hasPrincipalChartBasis_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor D hD) n

end Stacks.Conormal

end
